    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0361" n="273" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg273"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Wharton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic">March 21,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 17th of
                    March, inclosing a letter from the Lake Carriers’ Association on the subject of
                    discriminating <pb facs="0362" n="274" xml:id="pg274"/> tolls in the Canadian
                    canals, I have the honor to inform you that I have transmitted a copy of your
                    note and of its inclosure to the governor-general of Canada.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
